<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haydar Khan Amu-oghli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1880">1880</a>–<a href="/years/1921">1921</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Heydar Khan Amu-Oghli</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haydar Khan Amu-oghli was an Iranian revolutionary who took part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-constitutional-revolution">Persian Constitutional Revolution</a> and later led the Communist Party of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. In 1921 he was sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilan">Gilan</a> to reconcile the communists with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirza-kuchik-khan">Mirza Kuchik Khan</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jangal-movement">Jangali movement</a> in the Persian Socialist Soviet Republic. He was killed later that year in renewed fighting between the factions.</p></div>
